      "The Reynolds number is why a scale model in a wind tunnel tells you the truth about a real aircraft: match the dimensionless number and the fluid cannot tell the difference.",
      "Prandtl's boundary layer solved a 150-year-old paradox with one observation: viscosity is negligible everywhere except in a thin sheet at the surface, and that sheet is where the drag comes from.",
